Package: imprintomeR
Type: Package
Title: Quantitative Analysis and Visualization of Genomic Imprinting from DNA Methylation Arrays
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
        given = "Hongjian",
        family = "Jin",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        email = "hongjian.jin@stjude.org"
    )
Description: 
    imprintomeR provides a framework for quantitative analysis of genomic imprinting 
    using DNA methylation array data (Illumina 450K and EPIC platforms). The package 
    implements a continuous coordinate-based model to characterize imprinting states 
    using allele-aware methylation summaries. It supports probe-level, locus-level, 
    and cohort-level analysis, and includes visualization tools such as beeswarm plots, 
    mirror density plots, radar fingerprints, polar coordinate plots, and annotated heatmaps. 
    The package enables detection of imprinting deviations, directional mechanisms, 
    and epigenetic instability across samples.
